[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/entities/snow_load.gd" id="1_snowload"]

; The snow a walker is carrying: packed onto his boots by a drift, settled on his
; shoulders by the sky, shaken off by his own steps and melted off by warmth.
;
; A SCENE SO IT CAN BE DROPPED UNDER A BODY, and that is the whole of it: this
; node belongs to ONE walker, because the crust it drives is a material
; parameter on that walker's own mesh.
;
; It was an autoload, and an autoload cannot do this job. One global instance can
; whiten one body, and the reason this effect takes its footfalls off the
; EventBus rather than calling into the player is so the bear in Wave 4 and the
; hungry man in Wave 5 get snow on them for free. Free means adding this scene as
; a child of the bear -- no export to point, no service to register, no `.gd` to
; change -- and a single autoload could not have delivered any of it.
;
; Placed under the body rather than beside it in scenes/main.tscn for the same
; reason: it finds its subject by looking up, so where it sits IS the wiring.
; Both emitters still run in WORLD space and are still positioned by the footfall
; that made them; this node's own transform is nothing but a culling box, which
; its parent now carries between footfalls for free.

[node name="SnowLoad" type="Node3D" groups=["wind_consumer"]]
script = ExtResource("1_snowload")
